<div class="container">
    <hgroup>
        <h3>Senior Administrative Assistant</h3> 
        <time datetime="2021">2021</time>-<time datetime="2026">Present</time>
        <p>Pacific Coast Producers</p>
    </hgroup>
    <div class="content">
        <ul>
            <li>
                <h4>Systems & Reporting</h4>
                <ul>
                    <li>Proficient in JDE, QlikView, Smartsheet, Outlook, Microsoft Office, Syndigo, and Sysco Supplier Suite.</li>
                    <li>Generate monthly, quarterly, and annual accruals; run 30+ monthly sales reports, weekly warehouse/scorecard/YTD reports, and trend reports.</li>
                    <li>Compile weekly win reports and prepare monthly Sysco reports.</li>
                    <li>Reconcile corporate AMEX statements.</li>
                </ul>
            </li>
            <li>
                <h4>Administrative & Operational Support</h4>
                <ul>
                    <li>Manage sample requests: logging, submitting, tracking, and coordinating shipments.</li>
                    <li>Process invoices, submit to AR, and prepare check mailings.</li>
                    <li>Coordinate travel arrangements and create itineraries.</li>
                    <li>Organize major events including annual Chicago Broker Meeting and Foodservice Broker Plant Tours (50+ attendees).</li>
                    <li>Maintain and update Broker Tour Calendar and FS Broker Binder.</li>
                </ul>
            </li>
            <li>
                <h4>Sales & Business Support</h4>
                <ul>
                    <li>Prepare BID submissions: obtain approvals, apply pricing, and update BID sheets.</li>
                    <li>Support Business Analyst with broker reports, trend analysis, and warehouse reporting.</li>
                    <li>Maintain multiple supplier platforms and assist with NIF/Teamwork projects across Foodservice and Retail.</li>
                </ul>
            </li>
            <li>
                <h4>Marketing & Creative</h4>
                <ul>
                    <li>Create and update POS materials, flyers, sales sheets, and popup banners using InDesign.</li>
                    <li>Photograph products and enhance images using Photoshop.</li>
                    <li>Support website updates (WordPress) and contribute to crop reports and mock-ups.</li>
                    <li>Prepare booth materials and swag for trade shows and events; coordinate shipments</li>
                    <li>Film and prepare video content for management presentations.</li>
                </ul>
            </li>
            <li>
                <h4>Quality Assurance Support</h4>
                <ul>
                    <li>Obtain and submit QA documentation for customers; assist in maintaining food safety records.</li>
                    <li>Manage Label Destruction Tracking for Foodservice and Retail.</li>
                </ul>
            </li>
            <li>
                <h4>Executive & CrossFunctional Support</h4>
                <ul>
                    <li>Assist upper management with presentations, letters of support, swag preparation, and product pickups.</li>
                    <li>Support PowerPoint presentation development (images, animations, GIFs)</li>
                </ul>
            </li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</div>

<style>
    .container {
		container: about / inline-size;

    }
    .content {
        column-count: 2;
        column-width: 25rem;
        margin-inline-start: 25%;
        gap: 2rem;
        position: relative;
    }
    h2, h3, h4, hgroup {
        margin-bottom: 1rem;
    }
    ul:not(li ul) {
        list-style-type: none;
        padding: 0;
    }
    li ul {
        margin-block-end: 3rem;
        list-style-type: disc;
    }

    @container about (width < 80ch) {
        h2, h3, h4, hgroup {
            margin-bottom: 1rem;
        }
        .content {
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: column;
            gap: 2rem;
            margin-inline-start: 0;
        }
        li ul {
            margin-block-end: 2rem;
        }
    }
</style>

